    "created_at": "2025-04-17T18:42:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-17T18:42:23Z",
    "body": ">it seems quite clear to me where it talks about \"form[name]\"\n\nThat’s fair, it’s definitely clear once it clicks. But (admittedly), I often _search_ these documents first and I wasn’t getting any hits — but you could argue that _I’m doing it wrong_. I guess my thought would be to perhaps add a “Note” below the _interface_ tables to call out `getter (RadioNodeList or Element) (DOMString name)` or something.\n\nFor context, I am often wiring up forms inside a shadow root and so it’s pretty natural to want to set an `id` on my submit buttons of `\"submit\"`. I wonder if this sort of mistake may become more common as authoring elements with shadow roots becomes more prevalent 🤔\n\nI think you’re right that the current documentation covers it — I just didn’t digest what I was reading thoroughly enough 😞\n\nThanks so much (again!) for the quick responses. I’ll close this down and will drop a quick reference to the open thread about [opting out of this behavior in forms](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2212) (as I think that’s _really_ what I wish existed!).",
